      "findings": [
        {
          "confidence": 0.7,
          "evidence": "In v4.0.0 scripts/cvcore/usage.py, a parse error in last_cost_state is caught by the outer except and returns None. cost_state then returns None, so record() does nothing, and the restart branch is never reached that way. The $0 comes only from session_total() (transcript <= 8 MB with no parsed cost-state -> 0.0). hooks.py:256 uses session_total as the run-start baseline, so a new run gets credited the whole session once, not once per reading. Same root cause, same visible symptom (jump to the session cost), different route.",
          "file": "CHANGELOG.md",
          "id": "F1a",
          "line_end": 1,
          "line_start": 1,
          "recommendation": "Optional: reword to '4.0.0 can show the same jump through the run-start baseline.' Or leave as is: the user-visible claim (4.0.0 users are affected) is true.",
